  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  version: \"0.32.0.4\"\n\npackage:\n  name: wgpudawn\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://pypi.org/packages/source/w/wgpudawn/wgpudawn-${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: 285801512c52220c224e07a2a07452632aa9ed0c503c9f6b2078bb4ba3f9509c\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  # The cffi extension uses the limited API, so one build per platform covers\n  # all supported Python versions.\n  skip: not (match(python, python_min ~ \".*\") and is_abi3)\n  python:\n    version_independent: true\n  script:\n    # build_cffi.py looks for webgpu.h and the webgpu_dawn library in\n    # DAWN_PREFIX (and its Library/ on Windows); point it at the host prefix\n    # also when cross-compiling.\n    - if: unix\n      then: export DAWN_PREFIX=\"${PREFIX}\"\n      else: set \"DAWN_PREFIX=%PREFIX%\"\n    - ${{ PYTHON }} -m pip install . -vv --no-deps --no-build-isolation\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - if: build_platform != target_platform\n      then:\n        - python\n        - cross-python_${{ target_platform }}\n        - cffi >=1.17\n    - ${{ compiler('c') }}\n    - ${{ stdlib('c') }}\n    - ${{ compiler('cxx') }}\n  host:\n    - python\n    - python-abi3\n    - pip\n    - setuptools >=77\n    - cffi >=1.17\n    - dawn\n  run:\n    - python\n    - cffi >=1.17\n    # The extension uses Dawn's C++ API (dawn::native), which is not ABI\n    # stable, and Dawn has no run_exports; require the exact Dawn release.\n    - ${{ pin_compatible('dawn', upper_bound='x.x') }}\n    - if: osx\n      then:\n        - rubicon-objc >=0.4.1\n\ntests:\n  - python:\n      imports:\n        - wgpudawn\n        - wgpudawn.backends.dawn\n      python_version:\n        - ${{ python_min }}.*\n        - \"*\"\n  - requirements:\n      run:\n        - abi3audit\n    script:\n      - if: unix\n        then: abi3audit $SP_DIR/wgpudawn/_lib/_wgpu_dawn.abi3.so -s -v --assume-minimum-abi3 ${{ python_min }}\n        else: abi3audit %SP_DIR%\\wgpudawn\\_lib\\_wgpu_dawn.pyd -s -v --assume-minimum-abi3 ${{ python_min }}\n  - files:\n      source:\n        - tests/\n    requirements:\n      run:\n        - pip\n        - pytest\n        - numpy\n        - psutil\n        - imageio\n        - anyio\n        - trio\n        - rendercanvas >=2.4.0\n    script:\n      - pip check\n      - python -c \"import wgpudawn.backends.dawn as d; print(d.__version__)\"\n      # Tests that need a GPU adapter skip themselves when there is none.\n      - pytest tests -v\n\nabout:\n  homepage: https://github.com/hmaarrfk/wgpudawn\n  repository: https://github.com/hmaarrfk/wgpudawn\n  summary: WebGPU for Python, on Dawn. A standalone build of the wgpu-py API with a Dawn backend.\n  description: |\n    wgpudawn provides the wgpu-py API for WebGPU in Python, implemented on\n    top of Google's Dawn instead of wgpu-native. It is a cffi extension\n    linked against Dawn's webgpu.h and native C++ API.\n  license: BSD-2-Clause\n  license_file: LICENSE\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - hmaarrfk\n",
